WEBVTT

00:00.490 --> 00:02.020
Ten rounds total.

00:02.020 --> 00:07.680
One-on-one bouts of mathematics and
brawling held at the same time.

00:08.160 --> 00:12.810
The round ends when one side
solves the math problems.

00:12.810 --> 00:17.280
So unless you can finish the math
problems, the fight goes on forever.

00:17.280 --> 00:21.900
It's the only way to get bloodthirsty
adventurers to learn their arithmetic!

00:22.330 --> 00:25.810
Each problem set will be
tougher than the last.

00:25.810 --> 00:27.910
And at the start of the next round,

00:27.910 --> 00:30.590
for each 10-point difference in your scores,

00:30.590 --> 00:34.010
you get one free hit at the enemy brawler.

00:34.010 --> 00:36.310
That's a heavy responsibility.

00:36.830 --> 00:39.680
We'll use this to determine
the mathematics players.

00:42.670 --> 00:43.740
Huh?

00:43.740 --> 00:46.430
It's Curran.

00:46.430 --> 00:49.340
N-N-N-N-N!

00:48.100 --> 00:49.030
It's me, Nick.

00:49.030 --> 00:49.680
Calm down.

00:49.680 --> 00:52.190
I-I-I-I-I.

00:50.970 --> 00:52.940
Yes, you can do it.

00:52.940 --> 00:56.010
B-B-B-B-B!

00:54.410 --> 00:55.480
You'll be fine.

00:55.480 --> 00:56.730
Don't worry.

00:56.730 --> 00:58.450
How can he tell what she's saying?

00:58.670 --> 01:04.580
Hmph. I hope one screw-up
doesn't get everyone killed.

01:06.580 --> 01:09.970
U-U-U-U-U!

01:07.790 --> 01:09.300
She's saying "Uuuh."

01:09.960 --> 01:21.770
Ningen Fushin: Adventurers Who Don't
Believe in Humanity Will Save the World

02:40.720 --> 02:45.640
"Mathematics Bare Knuckle"

02:46.280 --> 02:47.420
Well?

02:47.420 --> 02:51.000
Hmm, I think she's got potential!

02:51.000 --> 02:52.350
What was my score?

02:53.330 --> 02:56.000
Curran, you worked hard, didn't you?

02:56.000 --> 02:58.350
Yup. So what was my score?

02:58.350 --> 03:01.250
If you did this good before you even
started studying, I think there's hope.

03:01.570 --> 03:02.360
What was my score?

03:02.750 --> 03:05.230
Curran, let the poor guy off the hook.

03:06.760 --> 03:08.240
It was no good?

03:09.460 --> 03:11.310
That's not true.

03:13.250 --> 03:16.880
Curran

03:15.540 --> 03:18.130
I can't do this.

03:18.130 --> 03:21.830
Curran, the most important thing right now

03:21.830 --> 03:26.940
is that we were able to see what
you can do and what you can't.

03:27.590 --> 03:30.370
So we just need to get you better
at the things you understand,

03:30.370 --> 03:33.490
and help you learn the things you don't.

03:34.750 --> 03:36.360
Can I do that?

03:36.360 --> 03:37.470
Of course.

03:42.510 --> 03:45.440
You should just let me help.

03:45.440 --> 03:49.160
Kizuna, you're too strong.

03:49.750 --> 03:53.840
But I want to help the Survivors, too.

03:54.990 --> 03:58.120
Of course, we want your help.

03:58.710 --> 03:59.810
Okay...

03:59.810 --> 04:03.770
Not as a sacred blade,
but as a party member.

04:04.640 --> 04:07.390
Leave it to me!

04:08.440 --> 04:12.820
We spent the next week training
and coming up with plans.

04:14.620 --> 04:17.850
Zem's been hanging out
with girls all day lately.

04:19.270 --> 04:22.090
Oh, Zem, you pervert!

04:22.580 --> 04:23.860
Eww!

04:23.860 --> 04:27.700
Why don't you stop wasting everybody's
time and get to the point?

04:28.690 --> 04:30.450
You knew, then?

04:31.050 --> 04:34.070
It's no fun to drink with
someone who's so glum.

04:34.070 --> 04:35.950
You've been like that all the time lately.

04:36.680 --> 04:39.190
All right, if you insist...

04:39.690 --> 04:43.390
I've heard more stories about that
Claudine girl breaking men's' hearts...

04:43.770 --> 04:47.410
Beg? The creepy guy, right?

04:47.410 --> 04:52.070
So Leon's not just strong,
he's pretty smart.

04:52.070 --> 04:54.330
The Iron Tigers went too far!

04:54.330 --> 05:00.080
Oh, that new girl, Rose, was
talking about some strange man.

05:00.830 --> 05:03.610
So you know something about a strange man?

05:03.960 --> 05:05.370
That's right.

05:05.370 --> 05:08.110
Can you tell me more?

05:09.520 --> 05:10.910
All right.

05:11.360 --> 05:12.740
Hmm...

05:13.100 --> 05:15.230
Wavy, flaxen hair,

05:15.230 --> 05:17.870
beautiful soft blue eyes...

05:18.210 --> 05:21.320
long, light pink fingers,

05:21.320 --> 05:23.880
a sexy voice like velvet...

05:23.880 --> 05:26.770
He wears a cassock that stands
out in a place like this...

05:26.770 --> 05:28.500
Who are you talking about?

05:29.210 --> 05:31.000
A strange man.

05:31.950 --> 05:35.640
They're going to try some
kind of trick tomorrow.

05:35.640 --> 05:36.820
Yeah.

05:36.820 --> 05:42.490
The way they acted, the way they lured
us into this, they've done it before.

05:42.490 --> 05:45.070
I've had Zem look into them.

05:45.070 --> 05:47.560
So he wasn't just out getting drunk?

05:47.560 --> 05:51.270
I had a lot to drink,
and asked lots of questions.

05:52.860 --> 05:55.620
He's cheating. I know it.

05:55.620 --> 05:58.040
But I can't figure out how.

05:58.040 --> 06:01.240
He's sharp, like he's got eyes
on the back of his head.

06:01.240 --> 06:03.480
And I can't figure it out!

06:04.280 --> 06:09.060
What they do is share information
so they can outsmart their enemy.

06:09.060 --> 06:12.420
They're probably using Thought Gems.

06:12.700 --> 06:15.060
Those work like telepathy, right?

06:15.060 --> 06:17.310
Not nearly as powerful, though.

06:17.310 --> 06:19.530
What do I do?

06:19.530 --> 06:23.820
Use all you've learned
to solve the problems.

06:23.820 --> 06:25.600
That's all?

06:25.600 --> 06:28.080
Until I give the signal.

06:31.130 --> 06:33.880
I was pretty happy as a kid.

06:34.430 --> 06:36.900
My parents worked at a carriage station,

06:36.900 --> 06:40.070
but started embezzling small
amounts of money and got fired.

06:43.630 --> 06:48.490
They were about to sell
me off when I ran away.

06:48.490 --> 06:51.010
But then I had to survive.

06:53.090 --> 06:56.520
I was pretty enough, which helped
me do enough fraud to live.

06:56.520 --> 06:59.730
I was smart enough to do
enough cons to get by.

06:59.730 --> 07:02.980
I met some decent enough guys
to earn a decent enough living.

07:03.560 --> 07:06.620
And that's when I met Nick.

07:06.620 --> 07:08.090
Happy Birthday!

07:08.090 --> 07:12.340
I thought that the more people I could
steal from, the happier I'd be.

07:13.210 --> 07:14.620
I just...

07:23.270 --> 07:25.910
I'll get you yet, Nick!

07:29.180 --> 07:32.470
Okay, let the Mathematics Bare Knuckle begin!

07:38.920 --> 07:39.960
I know these!

07:39.960 --> 07:42.170
They're the type of problems I've studied!

07:42.170 --> 07:45.250
Don't look so happy.

07:45.860 --> 07:47.790
These are problems a kid could do.

07:47.790 --> 07:49.410
Sh-Shut up.

07:50.070 --> 07:52.600
I'll finish this up fast to help Nick!

07:52.600 --> 07:54.120
Get him, Nick!

07:54.120 --> 07:55.980
Kick Leon's ass!

07:56.560 --> 07:59.380
This is a good opportunity for Curran.

07:59.790 --> 08:01.350
She looks like she's bad at math.

08:01.350 --> 08:05.870
They're not going to miss a chance
to take advantage of that.

08:07.740 --> 08:09.490
He's not taking the bait.

08:09.880 --> 08:11.140
Which means...

08:13.060 --> 08:14.880
He's not attacking.

08:14.880 --> 08:16.870
So he's buying time?

08:17.320 --> 08:19.160
This much was planned for...

08:20.910 --> 08:23.190
He's figured out some part of it.

08:23.190 --> 08:25.170
Good luck figuring out the rest!

08:25.170 --> 08:27.850
You'll never reach it without real smarts.

08:32.430 --> 08:34.680
Focus, Curran.

08:34.680 --> 08:38.410
What's important now is
getting the right answers!

08:40.860 --> 08:42.290
I-I'm done!

08:43.270 --> 08:45.760
Curran finished first!

08:45.760 --> 08:47.820
We will now begin the judging.

08:47.820 --> 08:50.120
Take a moment's break!

08:50.900 --> 08:54.620
Curran 86 Points, Claudine 98 points!

08:57.570 --> 09:00.770
Yeah, that's the problem with going fast.

09:00.770 --> 09:03.980
You get in such a rush that you get sloppy

09:03.980 --> 09:06.140
and end up losing points.

09:06.450 --> 09:09.260
You're better than I thought.

09:09.260 --> 09:11.490
Let's see how long you can last.

09:11.870 --> 09:14.010
S-Sorry, Nick!

09:14.010 --> 09:15.530
It's fine!

09:15.530 --> 09:19.280
Nobody gets worried about
a little pat from a kitty.

09:19.280 --> 09:21.460
Penalty time already?

09:22.710 --> 09:24.030
Here I go!

09:24.910 --> 09:26.420
Come on, kitty.

09:29.720 --> 09:32.420
Sorry, my hand slipped.

09:33.160 --> 09:35.310
So this is what you've
got up your sleeve...

09:35.310 --> 09:36.800
no, no, it's not.

09:38.500 --> 09:40.400
Don't you worry about it.

09:41.080 --> 09:44.950
What happens when you have to brawl
and do math at the same time?

09:44.950 --> 09:47.940
You might think the math is
there to preserve your stamina.

09:47.940 --> 09:51.400
You could try to save your brawler's strength

09:51.400 --> 09:54.100
by ending the math part fast,
like Curran tried to do.

09:54.100 --> 09:56.820
The math might seem less
important than the fighting,

09:56.820 --> 10:00.370
until you realize that you can use
it to go on the offensive, too!

10:01.840 --> 10:03.940
Round 2, start!

10:04.500 --> 10:08.280
Abusing the penalties
might not feel very nice,

10:08.280 --> 10:10.410
but it's a standard way to fight.

10:10.790 --> 10:13.720
Nothing's as effective as an attack
your opponent can't block.

10:14.490 --> 10:20.950
Especially, if your math player is good,
you can use it to get aggressive.

10:21.270 --> 10:25.180
Theoretically, if you could answer
every question instantly,

10:25.180 --> 10:28.600
you could inflict massive penalty
hits no matter how smart they were,

10:28.600 --> 10:31.800
since they wouldn't get to
answer a single question.

10:32.480 --> 10:36.110
It's not the brawlers who determine
the outcome of the game.

10:36.330 --> 10:39.250
Hence the attempts to buy time.

10:39.700 --> 10:42.700
And that's where they'll try to cheat.

10:43.290 --> 10:46.510
And so will we!

10:48.270 --> 10:51.750
Claudine 98, Curran 79!

10:52.440 --> 10:56.870
What a shame. I almost got him two hits.

10:59.800 --> 11:00.870
Curran!

11:01.960 --> 11:04.670
Wipe that look off your face.

11:04.670 --> 11:06.890
You're not the one getting hit.

11:06.890 --> 11:08.780
I know that!

11:08.780 --> 11:11.530
But... but...

11:11.830 --> 11:14.500
Don't worry about me.
Focus on the problems.

11:14.500 --> 11:17.940
But it's my fault you're being hit!

11:17.940 --> 11:20.040
Because I'm stupid!

11:20.040 --> 11:21.310
I'll tell you the truth...

11:22.400 --> 11:25.740
A week ago I couldn't even
imagine it would go like this.

11:25.740 --> 11:28.900
I was ready to take dozens of hits.

11:28.900 --> 11:30.530
But just count them.

11:30.530 --> 11:32.750
How many times have I been hit?

11:32.750 --> 11:35.010
T-Two.

11:35.010 --> 11:38.680
Yeah. You started off getting
80 percent of the questions wrong,

11:38.680 --> 11:42.140
and now you're a full-fledged
Mathematics Bare Knuckle player!

11:42.440 --> 11:45.630
You're giving it your best! I can tell!

11:45.940 --> 11:48.530
So don't call yourself stupid!

11:49.480 --> 11:53.230
But I might start getting more wrong.

11:53.230 --> 11:54.300
It's fine.

11:55.140 --> 11:56.620
That's fine.

11:56.620 --> 11:59.070
If you get one wrong, just use what you
learned to get it right next time.

11:59.070 --> 12:00.140
Nick...

12:00.650 --> 12:03.280
Curran, you're amazing!

12:06.020 --> 12:10.010
What are you so excited about?
This is simple arithmetic.

12:10.910 --> 12:14.900
I'm excited because I can do something
now that I couldn't before!

12:16.610 --> 12:19.760
I'll pretend I didn't hear all that.

12:19.760 --> 12:22.050
Any more talking and I'll treat
this as illegal stalling.

12:23.540 --> 12:26.050
Round 3! Start!

12:26.370 --> 12:28.650
Like I said, you're just some
Dragonian bumpkin who

12:28.650 --> 12:31.090
won't be able to solve
these problems for long!

12:35.400 --> 12:38.740
I was happy to be able to do
math I couldn't do before.

12:38.740 --> 12:41.770
But I couldn't let myself show
it because Nick was getting hit.

12:41.770 --> 12:44.940
But Nick was happy for my progress!

12:44.940 --> 12:47.440
So I won't hesitate anymore!

12:49.010 --> 12:52.930
If you want to run a con, you do it fast.

12:52.930 --> 12:56.080
Most people would do it
right after the start,

12:56.080 --> 12:59.080
and get things over and done with
before they had a chance to slip up.

12:59.470 --> 13:02.260
But there's a reason they didn't.

13:02.700 --> 13:07.280
Early in the game, you'd lose time repeating
the questions and answers to each other.

13:07.730 --> 13:08.840
Which means...

13:08.840 --> 13:13.110
They're trying to buy time and
let the problems get harder.

13:13.110 --> 13:16.480
When Curran stops being able
to blaze through the questions,

13:16.480 --> 13:19.710
they'll use the Thought Gems
to give Claudine a boost.

13:21.680 --> 13:24.070
I'm getting tired.

13:24.070 --> 13:28.370
If I want to use my speed to go on the
offensive, this is my last chance, but...

13:28.370 --> 13:30.340
Stop running around!

13:30.340 --> 13:32.100
Coward!

13:32.830 --> 13:34.780
Let the crowd say what they want.

13:34.780 --> 13:37.240
But buying time is part of our secret plan.

13:37.720 --> 13:40.630
I'll last as long as my strength holds out!

13:47.200 --> 13:48.560
That's strange...

13:48.560 --> 13:52.090
I'm not seeing any traces of magic use.

13:52.090 --> 13:54.140
Were we wrong?

13:54.460 --> 13:57.370
Or is there some other plan?

13:58.690 --> 14:01.400
The math's about to go beyond
what Curran learned.

14:01.820 --> 14:04.120
In the next round, she'll...

14:10.200 --> 14:13.290
Looks like I'll need to make more smoke.

14:27.860 --> 14:29.420
Vilma.

14:30.530 --> 14:31.670
What?

14:32.490 --> 14:34.800
This is just wasting everybody's time.

14:35.090 --> 14:37.550
Why don't we do all the
remaining problems at once?

14:37.840 --> 14:39.920
Our leader's tough enough to take it.

14:39.920 --> 14:41.310
Sounds like fun!

14:40.810 --> 14:43.090
Do it!

14:43.090 --> 14:48.040
You understand that means he'll take all
the penalty punches at once, right?

14:48.040 --> 14:49.580
Sounds good to me!

14:49.940 --> 14:52.700
I was going to say it if nobody else did.

14:52.700 --> 14:53.980
Nick...

14:54.320 --> 14:56.830
Is that woman stupid?

14:57.160 --> 15:01.090
He might be strong, but only for a human.

15:01.090 --> 15:07.090
With the damage he's taken,
does she think he can survive?

15:07.520 --> 15:10.990
If he's lucky, it'll put him in a coma.
If he's not, he's a dead man.

15:12.300 --> 15:14.300
Are they trying to stop us from buying time?

15:14.300 --> 15:15.480
But it's too late!

15:15.480 --> 15:17.390
Our plan's already complete!

15:17.390 --> 15:20.970
Your struggles will only
make it easier for us!

15:22.520 --> 15:25.320
I'll drive that alley cat from its hole!

15:26.320 --> 15:28.790
Now begin!

15:30.290 --> 15:32.030
Come on out, alley cat!

15:33.290 --> 15:35.580
I've solved all the problems so far on my own,

15:35.580 --> 15:38.270
but I can't let there be any
chance of me losing this.

15:40.110 --> 15:41.030
She's fast!

15:41.030 --> 15:43.110
Nice, Dragonian!

15:45.980 --> 15:47.000
She's bluffing.

15:47.310 --> 15:51.900
I've seen the scores she's gotten.
She doesn't really know any of this stuff.

15:51.900 --> 15:55.630
She's trying to pressure me by
writing wrong answers quickly.

15:55.630 --> 15:57.570
But this is my chance.

15:57.570 --> 15:59.890
I'll speed up and get through this.

16:00.240 --> 16:02.010
Beg, your turn.

16:02.370 --> 16:04.140
I've been waiting for this!

16:04.510 --> 16:06.610
We'll do these fast.

16:06.610 --> 16:10.890
First, 78+594/3.

16:11.550 --> 16:15.780
We've made a ton of money
with these Thought Gems,

16:15.780 --> 16:17.760
but it's too dangerous.

16:17.760 --> 16:19.300
This'll be the last time.

16:19.760 --> 16:22.200
And then I'll leave the Iron Tigers...

16:22.930 --> 16:27.170
Yeah. And then maybe I'll live a quiet,
normal life in some small town.

16:27.170 --> 16:29.040
You ready?

16:29.040 --> 16:30.050
Go.

16:30.050 --> 16:33.360
First is 2, 7, 6.

16:33.360 --> 16:36.130
Second is 3, 6, 8.

16:36.130 --> 16:37.560
The third is...

16:52.260 --> 16:56.050
So, I don't see the other member
of the Iron Tigers anywhere.

16:56.050 --> 16:57.500
He's not sick or anything, right?

16:58.300 --> 17:02.210
Oh, yeah. The guy said he had better
stuff to do than show up for this fight.

17:04.080 --> 17:07.790
Wait, that girl made a big fuss
about changing the rules.

17:08.100 --> 17:10.290
Where'd she go?

17:10.670 --> 17:12.530
Did they figure part of it out?

17:12.910 --> 17:14.560
No, it's impossible.

17:14.870 --> 17:17.080
Even if they did, it shouldn't matter.

17:17.080 --> 17:19.550
It shouldn't get them where they need to go.

17:20.010 --> 17:21.790
Why do I have this awful feeling...

17:25.880 --> 17:26.690
Don't tell me...

17:27.090 --> 17:28.560
This whole thing's a trap?

17:28.940 --> 17:30.430
Wait, Claudine!

17:30.860 --> 17:33.070
Shut up and don't talk to me!

17:33.420 --> 17:34.820
What are you talking about?

17:37.610 --> 17:39.390
It's too dangerous, Claudine!

17:39.790 --> 17:43.490
You're good enough at math to outwit
that Dragonian on your own, right?

17:44.330 --> 17:46.680
Give me the whole thing starting
from the second problem again.

17:46.680 --> 17:50.020
No, not that one. The one after 32.6!

17:50.650 --> 17:54.330
Damn it! Just give me
the answer to that one!

17:56.350 --> 17:59.340
I thought he'd be ruined
forever after I dumped him.

17:59.700 --> 18:01.960
But now he's back as an adventurer.

18:02.650 --> 18:03.890
What is he?

18:03.890 --> 18:06.000
What's that guy's deal?!

18:06.000 --> 18:08.130
This time, I'll get him hurt.

18:08.820 --> 18:14.100
Um, I'm redoing the problem after 32.6...

18:14.370 --> 18:16.920
So, um, wait...

18:15.860 --> 18:18.370
I can't bear to watch this anymore!

18:18.370 --> 18:20.670
That's the one Claudine wants!

18:20.670 --> 18:22.870
Oh, right! Thanks!

18:22.870 --> 18:24.100
Huh?

18:38.170 --> 18:42.630
Here's why you're an idiot: you let
Vilma hear you propose the duel!

18:44.420 --> 18:47.070
The guild's using this battle
for their own purposes.

18:47.900 --> 18:50.150
We've got the alley cat by the tail!

18:53.180 --> 18:54.500
He's taking too long!

18:54.500 --> 18:56.600
What the hell is Beg doing?

18:56.600 --> 18:57.910
Are you done yet?

18:57.910 --> 18:59.160
Answer me!

18:59.790 --> 19:02.130
You're taking too damn long!

19:04.840 --> 19:06.670
You're taking too long!

19:14.300 --> 19:17.610
Sorry, did we keep you waiting?

19:21.850 --> 19:24.290
Sorry, I messed up.

19:25.340 --> 19:26.270
Idiot.

19:26.860 --> 19:29.440
So here's your tail.

19:31.030 --> 19:35.460
That's a Thought Gem. I'm sure of it.

19:36.220 --> 19:38.780
You've got one, too, don't you, Claudine?

19:40.850 --> 19:43.820
I got a little worried when I
couldn't pick up any magic.

19:43.820 --> 19:46.630
Sheesh... You waited too
long to try and cheat.

19:46.630 --> 19:47.510
What?

19:47.510 --> 19:49.370
They were cheating?

19:50.650 --> 19:52.520
Too bad.

19:52.520 --> 19:57.800
I was hoping you might continue
a fair fight until the end.

19:57.800 --> 19:59.450
You screwed up, big time.

20:03.160 --> 20:04.460
When?

20:05.780 --> 20:07.810
When did you figure it out?

20:07.810 --> 20:11.490
We knew from the start
that you were bad people!

20:11.490 --> 20:13.910
Curran, that's not what he meant.

20:13.910 --> 20:15.340
When?

20:19.000 --> 20:22.110
I wasn't a bad person to start with!

20:25.790 --> 20:29.840
I wasn't a bad person to start with, either!

20:29.840 --> 20:31.230
That's enough, Claudine.

20:31.230 --> 20:32.610
I wasn't...

20:33.230 --> 20:35.470
We're finished.

20:35.470 --> 20:37.540
I wanted to believe, too...

20:38.250 --> 20:40.960
I wanted to believe!

20:42.060 --> 20:44.380
Nobody's a bad person to start with.

20:45.120 --> 20:47.290
Maybe you went off the right path somewhere,

20:47.290 --> 20:49.160
but I don't have the right
to say that to you.

20:49.520 --> 20:54.490
'Cause sometimes maybe it's wrong,
but you feel like you don't have a choice.

20:54.890 --> 20:59.420
But if you realize you made a mistake,
you can go back and fix it.

21:00.710 --> 21:04.580
You can't start over, but you
can correct your mistakes.

21:05.300 --> 21:08.860
That's what I've been telling myself lately.

21:12.790 --> 21:17.840
ELUSIVE AND STRANGE!
A mysterious creature appears!

21:14.380 --> 21:17.850
A mysterious, elusive creature
appears in the Labyrinth City.

21:17.850 --> 21:19.650
Seems neat!

21:19.650 --> 21:22.710
You can't waste time on every
weird thing out there.

21:22.710 --> 21:24.460
Oh? Are you scared?

21:24.820 --> 21:28.470
No, I don't mean the creature,
I mean the article.

21:28.800 --> 21:31.220
Don't believe that garbage.

21:32.000 --> 21:33.940
You're so boring.

21:33.940 --> 21:37.110
Nick's more of a realist than I thought.

21:38.190 --> 21:39.530
Hey, Nick.

21:39.530 --> 21:43.720
If I didn't need to get the right answers,
was there any reason for me to study?

21:44.580 --> 21:46.430
It's not that simple.

21:46.430 --> 21:49.510
We were only able to win in
the end because you showed

21:49.510 --> 21:51.480
what you could do at the start.

21:51.830 --> 21:53.390
You did a good job, Curran.

21:54.860 --> 21:57.000
Y-Yeah?

21:57.000 --> 22:01.230
And I think what you've learned
will help in your daily life, too.

22:01.630 --> 22:03.410
W-Will it?

22:04.700 --> 22:09.130
You might be able to tell at a glance who's
got the best deal on the extra-large size!

22:09.130 --> 22:11.510
Oh, that's handy!

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
Next time:
"Gambling Lesson"

23:36.140 --> 23:39.140
Next time: "Gambling Lesson".
